A||||5||RobH||Bad fuel pump, can it cause flooding?||||5||
Z||000000||RobH||09-17-2000||12:15 PM||||Got a problem with starting my 86 SE V6. It may take 10 or so sec to start, and then I smell very "rich" fumes, as if the engine is flooding. (this happens whether hot or cold if it sits for more than 5 or 10 minutes)  I figured it maybe the Cold Start Valve.  I unplugged it and it doesn't take as long (I figure because it is not squirting more fuel into flooded engine, with cold start it takes a couple secs longer to start).<P>I thought it may also be leaking injectors, but I went and bought a fuel pressure tester and am getting 41psi when fuel pump turns on.  It slowly leaks down.  Then I pinched the Fuel Pressure Line and pressure holds *longer*, but still leaks slowly, which tells me that I may also have a faulty fuel pump or pulsator or a leak somewhere down in the tank.<P>My question is, can a faulty fuel pump cause these kinds of problems with flooding?<P>I may still check the injectors, but do not want to pull the topside if I don't have too.<P>UPDATE:<BR>I just pulled the topside and checked the injectors, they appear to be ok, or at least they aren't leaking much at all ( I can't see any fuel dripping out of injectors ).  Pressure continues to drop very slowly though.  I have the fuel pressure line pinched as well.<P>Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>Thanks...<BR>Rob<p>[This message has been edited by RobH (edited 09-17-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-17-2000||05:48 PM||||Did you check the cold start injector for leakage also? ||||reg||5
Z||000002||N_Man||09-17-2000||08:37 PM||||Im pretty interested in the solution because my car has nearly identical symptoms||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||09-17-2000||10:23 PM||||It wont be the cold start switch, because it only works when the starter is engaged. sounds like the fuel pressure regulator.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||09-17-2000||10:23 PM||||It wont be the cold start switch, because it only works when the starter is engaged. sounds like the fuel pressure regulator.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RobH||09-17-2000||11:14 PM||||Update:<BR>I replaced all the fuel injectors, seems the leaky injector(s) leaked very slowly.  After replacing them, the car starts right up.  I even hooked the Cold Start valve backup and it works fine ( it did not leak ).<P>I still need to replace the fuel pump though, as it does not maintain pressure when the fuel pressure line is *not* pinched during the pressure test.  I figure that job is a weekender though...so maybe next weekend.<P>The true test to whether or not replacing the injectors works, will be in the morning after it has sat all night.||||reg||1
